WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.935
If machine words sound natural above a certain width, why not switch at that number?

q0002
00:00:08.935 --> 00:00:19.447
This episode has one job: A simple width-only flat-versus-words rule failed its declared regret gate, showing that support width is one feature rather than a universal selector.

q0003
00:00:19.447 --> 00:00:29.959
We build on Packed truth vectors: big integers, machine words, and masks, Preparation, kernel, wrapper, and end-to-end time; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:29.959 --> 00:00:40.015
A selector chooses an engine from pre-execution features and must control regret on the declared evaluation set.

q0005
00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:48.389
Watch for the label selector; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:56.203
When we say regret, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:56.203 --> 00:01:06.259
The term validation reuse receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
